host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "The `ctx` parameter is genuinely dead in `on_save` (callers already log to `ctx` themselves), so the right fix is removing it rather than renaming to `_ctx` or adding `noqa`.\npytest isn't installed, so I ran the test function directly:\nI fixed the failure, and `make lint` now reports \"All checks passed!\".\n\n**Cause:** In `notes/hooks.py`, the `on_save(doc, ctx)` function never used its `ctx` argument. Its two callers, `save` and `autosave`, already write to `ctx` themselves before calling it.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the argument, so the function is now `on_save(doc)`, and updated both calls to match. Nothing else in the repo calls `on_save`. I didn't hide the warning by renaming the argument to `_ctx` or adding a `noqa` comment, because the argument really was unused.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `make test` won't run here because pytest isn't installed, so I ran `tests/test_hooks.py::test_save_and_autosave` directly and it passed.\n- I also checked by hand that passing a `ctx` list to `save` and `autosave` still records `[('save', 'b'), ('autosave', 'b')]`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 3, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 233938, "requests_cache_write": 72776, "requests_cost_usd": 0.4394076, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 1433, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-unusedparam:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 3, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-12T23:48:02.656974+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 25.329, "t_checker_s": 0.38, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "t